entry='<article class="paper-row" id="energy-admission-v01"><div class="paper-number">G20</div><div><span class="eyebrow">Conditional theorem manuscript · development 0.1</span><h2>Energy admission with norm and Gauss residuals</h2><p>A joint geometry-and-energy gate admits preparations beyond the earlier sufficient distance-only ball.</p><p class="muted">Conserved norm errors spend a centered curvature budget. Ambient Hamiltonian confinement holds at nonzero Gauss levels, with an explicit residual envelope; unequal norms still preclude closed-carrier zero-source neutrality. A frozen residual-cone example rules out a linear correction estimate. An exact zero-Gauss witness is admitted at 2.5 times the earlier sufficient radius. Forty-nine exact checks and separately typed matrix diagnostics pass. Independent review pending; physical promotion 0. No constraint repair or physical calibration is implied.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="'+link+files[2]+'">Read theorem PDF ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="'+link+z.name+'">Proof and input contract ↓</a><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=ERA01">Claims and scope →</a></div></div></article>'
